"citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c5"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c5"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c5","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.71 (Induction from the depth-six example)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.71, p. 64, label record:257bm-c5","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*An already-formalised induction from the endpoint-six seed (Definition 6.97) consumes Theorem 6.70 at every step: each protected exact row either doubles below half (unconditional) or recycles at its first crossing rank $e >$ cutoff, giving endpoint $2e-2 >$ previous endpoint; protection (endpoint $< 2\\cdot$cutoff, new ranks $>$ cutoff) is exactly what converts the non-growing recycle endpoint of the bare dichotomy (Theorem 6.127) into strict progress. The below-half branch never fires twice from the seed arithmetic, so the supply is needed at essentially every step. Its conclusion is the cofinal exact-row condition of Definition 6.66.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c5","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c5","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c5%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c5%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257